{% set local_problem %}
<p>Meridianville's sloped terrain is a double-edged sword for drainage. On one hand, gravity wants to move water downhill — good. On the other hand, if your home sits on that slope, water from uphill runs toward you — bad.</p>

<p>Many Meridianville homes have downspouts that dump water right next to the foundation, where it has nowhere to go but into your crawlspace or basement. Splash blocks help a little, but they can't overcome physics — water still pools too close to the house.</p>

<p>Underground drains solve this problem permanently. They capture water from your downspouts and carry it through buried pipes to a safe discharge point far from your foundation. On sloped lots, we use the terrain to our advantage, routing pipes downhill where gravity does the work.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drains are buried pipes that connect to your downspouts and carry water to a discharge point away from your home. The system typically includes: catch basins at each downspout that collect water and filter debris; solid PVC pipe buried underground; proper slope (typically 1/8 inch per foot minimum) to ensure flow; and a discharge point — either daylight, dry well, or storm drain connection.</p>

<p>We assess your property's terrain, identify the best discharge locations, and design a system that uses gravity effectively. The result is complete, invisible water management from your roof to a safe exit point.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>Underground drain installation requires understanding drainage — not just digging trenches. We've installed these systems throughout Meridianville and know how to work with the area's terrain.</p>

<p>As your neighbors just 12 miles away in Huntsville, we're accountable for our work. If something isn't right, we're close by to fix it.</p>
{% endset %}

